{"name":"Hokey Pokey","hex":"#bb8e34","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hokey Pokey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A group dance performed in a circle, in which people move a variety of their body parts in and out of the middle, and shake them about."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hokey_Pokey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hokey pokey (ice cream)","blocks":[{"text":"Hokey pokey is a flavour of ice cream in New Zealand and Australia consisting of plain vanilla ice cream with small, solid lumps of honeycomb toffee. Hokey pokey is the New Zealand term for honeycomb toffee. The original recipe until around 1980 consisted of solid toffee, but in a marketing change, Tip Top decided to use small balls of honeycomb toffee instead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Honeycomb_ice_cream_and_hot_toffee_sauce_%285725734559%29.jpg/330px-Honeycomb_ice_cream_and_hot_toffee_sauce_%285725734559%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hokey_pokey_(ice_cream)","wikidata":"Q5878001"},{"title":"Hokey Pokey (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hokey Pokey is the second album by the British duo of singer Linda Thompson and singer/songwriter/guitarist Richard Thompson. It was recorded in the autumn of 1974 and released in the year 1975."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Hokey_Pokey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hokey_Pokey_(album)","wikidata":"Q5877998"},{"title":"Hokey Cokey","blocks":[{"text":"The Hokey Cokey is a participation dance with a distinctive accompanying tune and lyric structure. It is well-known in English-speaking countries. It originates in a British folk dance, with variants attested as early as 1826. The song and accompanying dance peaked in popularity as a music hall song and novelty dance in the mid-1940s in the UK. The song became a chart hit twice in the 1980s. The first UK hit was by The Snowmen, which peaked at UK No. 18 in 1981."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Pickering_War_Weekend_%2810254453475%29.jpg/330px-Pickering_War_Weekend_%2810254453475%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hokey_Cokey","wikidata":"Q3643110"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Sèvres - Magot - Pajou, buste de Madame du Barry 08","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/S%C3%A8vres_-_Magot_-_Pajou%2C_buste_de_Madame_du_Barry_08.jpg/500px-S%C3%A8vres_-_Magot_-_Pajou%2C_buste_de_Madame_du_Barry_08.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%A8vres_-_Magot_-_Pajou,_buste_de_Madame_du_Barry_08.jpg","share":0.14875},{"title":"Gordon Brown (2008)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Gordon_Brown_%282008%29.jpg/500px-Gordon_Brown_%282008%29.jpg","ratio":0.7823681298413869,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gordon_Brown_(2008).jpg","share":0.11125},{"title":"Hokey pokey ice cream (cropped)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Hokey_pokey_ice_cream_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Hokey_pokey_ice_cream_%28cropped%29.jpg","ratio":1.2432950191570882,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hokey_pokey_ice_cream_(cropped).jpg","share":0.081875},{"title":"Alumnae Hall, Brown University","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Alumnae_Hall%2C_Brown_University.jpg/500px-Alumnae_Hall%2C_Brown_University.jpg","ratio":1.7751479289940828,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alumnae_Hall,_Brown_University.jpg","share":0.075},{"title":"Port Broughton Hotel 20260127-123706","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Port_Broughton_Hotel_20260127-123706.jpg/500px-Port_Broughton_Hotel_20260127-123706.jpg","ratio":0.7